# Robot builder

The [Robot Builder](/robot) lets you assemble a basic FGC 2026 robot configuration and save it to your account.

## Configure a build

Give your robot a recognizable name, then select options across the three configuration areas:

- **Drive** — choose a drivetrain such as Mecanum, Tank, Swerve, or H-Drive.
- **Intake** — select a roller claw, over-the-bumper intake, or no intake.
- **Scoring** — select a flywheel, catapult, puncher, or no scoring mechanism.

The panel also shows a simple configuration preview and estimated specifications. These are visual guidance for the current prototype, not official FIRST Global robot rules or engineering limits.

## Save your robot

Select **Save build** after configuring your robot. The simulator stores the name and selected module data under your account.

A confirmation message appears after the save succeeds. If saving fails, check your connection, sign in again if needed, and retry.

## Saved builds

Saved robots appear in the list on the builder page, with their most recent update date. The latest saved robot is used by the existing match-ticket API when the game server requests a player build.

> Build persistence is available now. The interactive browser match-joining flow that uses those builds is not yet published.
